  "blocks": [
    {
      "text": "You can configure the scan rule to scan Azure Databricks workspaces. DSPM scans these resources for any sensitive data and vulnerabilities and displays the scan results on the Resource Inventory page."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Prerequisites",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "text": "Before configuring the scan rule, you need to configure the Databricks workspaces. To learn more, see About Service Registration."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Configuring Scan Rule",
      "level": 1
    },
    {
      "text": "To configure a scan rule for Databricks workspaces, complete the following steps in the Zscaler Admin Console:"
    },
    {
      "item": "1. Provide the general information.",
      "depth": 0
    },
    {
      "item": "From the navigation menu, go to Data Security > DSPM > Scan Settings.",
      "depth": 1,
      "number": 1,
      "strong": [
        [
          32,
          45
        ],
        [
          48,
          52
        ],
        [
          55,
          68
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "Select the Scan Rules tab.",
      "depth": 1,
      "number": 2,
      "strong": [
        [
          11,
          21
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "If you are configuring the scan rule for the first time, the following page appears:",
      "depth": 1
    },
    {
      "item": "See image.",
      "depth": 1
    },
    {
      "item": "Click Add Scan Rule.",
      "depth": 1,
      "number": 3,
      "strong": [
        [
          6,
          19
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "See image.",
      "depth": 1
    },
    {
      "item": "The General Information page appears.",
      "depth": 1,
      "strong": [
        [
          4,
          23
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "On the General Information page:",
      "depth": 1,
      "number": 4,
      "strong": [
        [
          7,
          26
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "Scan Rule Name: Enter a unique and descriptive name for the scan rule.",
      "depth": 2,
      "number": 1,
      "strong": [
        [
          0,
          14
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "Scan Rule Description (Optional): Enter a description of the scan rule (maximum 500 characters).",
      "depth": 2,
      "number": 2,
      "strong": [
        [
          0,
          32
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "See image.",
      "depth": 1
    },
    {
      "item": "Click Next.",
      "depth": 1,
      "number": 5,
      "strong": [
        [
          6,
          10
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "2. Select the cloud and resource type.",
      "depth": 0
    },
    {
      "item": "On the Select Cloud and Resource Type page:",
      "depth": 1,
      "number": 1,
      "strong": [
        [
          7,
          37
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "Cloud Type: Select Azure.",
      "depth": 2,
      "strong": [
        [
          0,
          10
        ],
        [
          19,
          24
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "Resource Category: Select Database.",
      "depth": 2,
      "strong": [
        [
          0,
          17
        ],
        [
          26,
          34
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "Resource Type: Select Databricks.",
      "depth": 2,
      "strong": [
        [
          0,
          13
        ],
        [
          22,
          32
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "See image.",
      "depth": 1
    },
    {
      "item": "Click Next.",
      "depth": 1,
      "number": 2,
      "strong": [
        [
          6,
          10
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "3. Select the resources that must be scanned.",
      "depth": 0
    },
    {
      "item": "On the Select Resources to Scan page, choose one of the following options:",
      "depth": 1,
      "number": 1,
      "strong": [
        [
          7,
          31
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "Scan All Resources: Scan all the resources across all onboarded and future workspaces and catalogs.",
      "depth": 2,
      "strong": [
        [
          0,
          18
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "Scan Specific Resources: Select the checkbox for specific workspaces and catalogs that must be scanned.",
      "depth": 2,
      "strong": [
        [
          0,
          23
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "See image.",
      "depth": 1
    },
    {
      "item": "Click Next.",
      "depth": 1,
      "number": 2,
      "strong": [
        [
          6,
          10
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "4. Select the scan type.",
      "depth": 0
    },
    {
      "item": "On the Scan Type page, select Data Sampling Scan to scan a sample of recent data in the workspace.",
      "depth": 1,
      "number": 1,
      "strong": [
        [
          7,
          16
        ],
        [
          30,
          48
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "DSPM cannot detect files that are deleted from the Databricks workspace.",
      "depth": 1
    },
    {
      "item": "See image.",
      "depth": 1
    },
    {
      "item": "Click Next.",
      "depth": 1,
      "number": 2,
      "strong": [
        [
          6,
          10
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "5. Set up the scan schedule.",
      "depth": 0
    },
    {
      "item": "On the Scan Schedule page:",
      "depth": 1,
      "number": 1,
      "strong": [
        [
          7,
          20
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "On Demand (Default): Scan the data manually when needed.",
      "depth": 2,
      "strong": [
        [
          0,
          9
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "Daily: Scan the data daily.",
      "depth": 2,
      "strong": [
        [
          0,
          5
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "Weekly: Scan the data once a week. Select the day from the drop-down menu.",
      "depth": 2,
      "strong": [
        [
          0,
          6
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "Monthly: Scan the data once a month.",
      "depth": 2,
      "strong": [
        [
          0,
          7
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "See image.",
      "depth": 1
    },
    {
      "item": "Click Next.",
      "depth": 1,
      "number": 2,
      "strong": [
        [
          6,
          10
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "6. Select the scan scope.",
      "depth": 0
    },
    {
      "item": "On the Scan Scope page, choose a scan scope from the drop-down menu.",
      "depth": 1,
      "number": 1,
      "strong": [
        [
          7,
          17
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "To learn more about configuring and creating a scan scope, see Configuring Scan Scope.",
      "depth": 1
    },
    {
      "item": "See image.",
      "depth": 1
    },
    {
      "item": "Click Next.",
      "depth": 1,
      "number": 2,
      "strong": [
        [
          6,
          10
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "7. Review and complete the configuration.",
      "depth": 0
    },
    {
      "item": "Review the scan settings. Click the Edit icon to change any values, if needed.",
      "depth": 1,
      "number": 1,
      "strong": [
        [
          36,
          40
        ]
      ]
    },
    {
      "item": "See image.",
      "depth": 1
    },
    {
      "item": "Click Finish.",
      "depth": 1,
      "number": 2,
      "strong": [
        [
          6,
          12
        ]
      ]
    }
  ]
}
